DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: what a chain does.
# Model: Chain drive (motor A turns the 16-tooth sprocket; a Technic chain runs round it
# and the 24-tooth sprocket five holes further on).
# A chain turns both sprockets the SAME way (two gears that touch turn opposite ways).
# The big sprocket has 24 teeth to the small one's 16, so it turns slower: 3 turns of
# the motor make 2 turns of the big sprocket.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor speed A 50
  start motor A forward
  display text "3:2"
  wait 4 seconds
  stop motor A
  set motor speed A 50
  start motor A backward
  display text "back"
  wait 3 seconds
  stop motor A
